{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement all code in Go, consistent with the existing Hyperledger Fabric codebase, using gRPC/Protocol Buffers for service and chaincode interfaces.",
    "U1: The friendly name is an immutable, human-readable label stored in the chaincode identity/deployment metadata, surfaced in peer logs and CLI output; it is not a security identity and uniqueness is scoped per channel/ledger.",
    "U2: Lifecycle management is implemented as a system chaincode (LSCC) invoked via signed proposals; deployment/upgrade policies are evaluated by reusing the existing endorsement/validation (ESCC/VSCC) policy framework rather than building a new policy engine.",
    "U4: The Solo orderer is a standalone minimal process exposing the atomic broadcast API (Broadcast and Deliver gRPC services). Clients submit envelopes that are multiplexed into a buffered channel; a single consenter thread performs block cutting based on batch size and a batch timeout. Deliver supports disconnection/reconnection via seek over a simple in-memory (RAM) block ledger with per-client cursors; no crash persistence is provided since the scope is development/testing.",
    "U5: Source availability on GitHub is achieved with a read-only mirror using Gerrit's replication plugin; GitHub is not a contribution path (Gerrit remains authoritative).",
    "U6: The state cache sits between the transaction simulator/query executor and the versioned state database (RocksDB). It is a size-bounded, concurrency-safe LRU cache of committed state used to build read-write sets faster; entries are invalidated at block commit time; the cache is configurable and can be disabled.",
    "U8: Peer CLI commands are extracted into a standalone module that depends only on client-facing protobuf definitions and lightweight client helpers, with no dependency on peer internals or RocksDB. Static cross-compiled binaries (CGO disabled) are produced for Linux, macOS, and Windows.",
    "Documentation is authored in reStructuredText/Markdown, built with Sphinx, published via Read the Docs, and linked from hyperledger.org (U3, U7)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The work is performed by a single experienced Go developer already familiar with the Fabric codebase; estimates cover design, implementation, unit/integration testing, documentation, and code-review rework for each item.",
    "A working Fabric development environment, Gerrit repository, and CI infrastructure already exist; no environment procurement or licensing effort is required.",
    "The Solo orderer targets development/test use only: no persistent ledger, no crash recovery guarantees, and no multi-process consensus are required, consistent with the specification.",
    "U5 effort covers one-time mirror configuration and verification; ongoing synchronization is automated and adds no recurring development effort.",
    "U7 covers publishing, structure, and discoverability of documentation only; authoring the upgrade-flow content itself is covered by U3.",
    "U6 performance goals are validated with micro-benchmarks and integration tests; no formal performance certification or production hardening is included.",
    "The extracted CLI (U8) preserves existing peer command behavior and flags; server-side changes are limited to what the CLI requires.",
    "Estimates are effort (work-hours), not elapsed time; they exclude project management, meetings, and organizational overhead."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Design chaincode friendly-name scheme",
      "activity_description": "Define where the friendly name is stored (chaincode identity/deployment metadata), validation rules, and how it appears in logs and CLI output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement friendly name in chaincode lifecycle and shim",
      "activity_description": "Add the friendly-name field to chaincode deployment data structures and the chaincode shim so it is propagated on deploy/instantiate and available for management/debugging.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - CLI/log integration and tests",
      "activity_description": "Surface the friendly name in peer CLI commands and log statements; add unit tests covering naming, validation, and display.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.1",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Design lifecycle system chaincode (LSCC)",
      "activity_description": "Specify LSCC API (deploy/upgrade/query), on-ledger data model for chaincode definitions, and integration points with the policy framework.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Implement LSCC chaincode",
      "activity_description": "Implement the LSCC system chaincode: storing/retrieving chaincode definitions, deploy and upgrade invocation handling, and query support.",
      "most_likely_effort": 64
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Deployment policy enforcement integration",
      "activity_description": "Wire LSCC operations to signed-proposal validation and the endorsement/validation policy framework so deployment and upgrade policies are evaluated and enforced.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2.4",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Peer system chaincode wiring and tests",
      "activity_description": "Register LSCC with the peer's system chaincode provider, integrate with the endorsement flow, and add unit and integration tests for deploy/upgrade/policy paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.1",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Write upgrade flow documentation",
      "activity_description": "Author documentation describing chaincode upgrade flows end to end, including commands, policy considerations, and worked examples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3.2",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Review and publish upgrade docs",
      "activity_description": "Incorporate review feedback, verify examples against a running network, and publish the documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.1",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Solo orderer scaffolding, configuration, and gRPC endpoints",
      "activity_description": "Create the standalone orderer process, configuration loading, and skeleton Broadcast/Deliver gRPC service implementations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.2",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Broadcast path and message validation",
      "activity_description": "Implement client envelope ingestion with basic validation, multiplexing multiple client streams into a buffered channel for the consenter.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.3",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Solo consenter with batching and block cutting",
      "activity_description": "Implement the single-threaded consenter that drains the channel and cuts blocks based on batch size and batch timeout, with no multi-process consensus.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - In-memory RAM ledger",
      "activity_description": "Implement a simple in-RAM block ledger storing cut blocks, providing append and indexed retrieval to support deliver/history.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Deliver service with seek and reconnect support",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Deliver gRPC service allowing clients to seek within ledger history (oldest/newest/specific block) so disconnected clients can resume.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4.6",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Solo orderer unit and integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Add unit tests for batching, block cutting, ledger, and seek behavior, plus integration tests with multiple concurrent clients including disconnect/reconnect scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 56
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.1",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Configure Gerrit to GitHub mirror",
      "activity_description": "Set up and configure replication from Gerrit to a read-only GitHub mirror repository and verify initial synchronization of the Fabric code.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5.2",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Validate ongoing sync and update contributor docs",
      "activity_description": "Verify ongoing push synchronization, document the read-only nature of the GitHub mirror, and update contributor documentation to reference it.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.1",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Design state cache",
      "activity_description": "Define cache semantics: what is cached, invalidation at block commit, size bounding (LRU), concurrency model, and configuration options.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.2",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Implement state cache and integrate with tx simulator",
      "activity_description": "Implement the concurrency-safe, size-bounded cache and integrate it between the transaction simulator/query executor and the versioned state database to accelerate rw-set construction.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.3",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Commit-time invalidation and configuration",
      "activity_description": "Hook cache invalidation/refresh into the block commit path to guarantee correctness, and expose cache sizing/enablement via peer configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6.4",
      "activity_name": "U6 - State cache benchmarks and tests",
      "activity_description": "Add unit tests (including concurrency and invalidation correctness), integration tests, and micro-benchmarks demonstrating rw-set build performance improvement.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.1",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Set up documentation publishing",
      "activity_description": "Configure Sphinx/Read the Docs build and publishing pipeline and a discoverable landing entry point linked from hyperledger.org.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7.2",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Restructure documentation index and links",
      "activity_description": "Organize the documentation index and cross-links for chaincode and application developers, and verify all links and published output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.1",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Extract CLI into standalone module",
      "activity_description": "Move peer CLI commands into a separate component that depends only on client-facing protobufs and lightweight client helpers, removing dependencies on peer internals and RocksDB.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.2",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Cross-platform build and packaging",
      "activity_description": "Set up static cross-compilation (CGO disabled) and packaging to produce simply installable platform-specific binaries for Linux, macOS, and Windows.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8.3",
      "activity_name": "U8 - CLI tests and installation documentation",
      "activity_description": "Add CLI unit/functional tests verifying command parity with the original peer commands, and write installation and usage documentation for the standalone binary.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9.1",
      "activity_name": "Increment integration and end-to-end regression",
      "activity_description": "Integrate all increment features, run end-to-end scenarios (deploy/upgrade with friendly names via LSCC, solo orderer networks, CLI against components, cache-enabled peers), update CI jobs, and fix integration defects.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 696
  }
}

